PINENTRY(1)

# NAME

pinentry - wrapper for secure PIN entry dialogs

# SYNOPSIS

*pinentry* [options]

# DESCRIPTION

*pinentry* is a wrapper script that selects an available PIN entry
frontend at runtime.
It is invoked by *gpg-agent*(1) and other GnuPG components to securely
prompt for passphrases.

The wrapper checks for installed frontends in the following order:

- *pinentry-qt5*
- *pinentry-qt*
- *pinentry-gtk-2*
- *pinentry-gnome3*
- *pinentry-curses*

The first available binary is executed with all arguments passed
through unchanged.
If no frontend is found, *pinentry* exits with status 1 and prints an
error message.

# CONFIGURATION

A specific frontend may be forced by adding a directive to
_gpg-agent.conf_:

```
pinentry-program /usr/bin/pinentry-curses
```

# EXIT STATUS

*0*
	Command executed successfully.

*>0*
	An error occurred.

# FILES

_~/.gnupg/gpg-agent.conf_
	Configuration file for *gpg-agent*(1), which may specify the
	*pinentry-program* directive.

# NOTES

This wrapper script and its man page are not part of the upstream
*pinentry* distribution.
They are provided by the Zeppe-Lin package to ensure consistent
behavior and documentation.

Upstream *pinentry* does not ship man pages for individual frontends.
All frontend stubs redirect to this page.
Arguments for each frontend can be inspected with:

```
pinentry-frontend --help
```

# SEE ALSO

*gpg-agent*(1)

